This is a full 32bit color script. I don't know if it works, I'm posting it for the license.
Licensed Under Creative Commons Attribution Non-Commercial Open Source

What it's supposed to do: Take full sized cells and make tiny color cells inside of the 16x16 half cells so it fills up the screen with full resolution imagemagick.
It should not require awk.

It's all supposed render in gamma with the nano64 color filter. So I added a 32bit layer. So gamma - nano64 16bit - 32bit filter.

NEW 
7/9/2026

Command for ai_cells.sh
convert image.jpg -resize WxH txt:-

How it fits into the pipeline

convert img.jpg -resize ... txt:- > pixels.txt
ai_cells.sh pixels.txt > display.txt
zc_validate < display.txt
zc_raster_schema.sh display.txt
zc_pulse_loop.sh display.txt
